Subject: clients: return main()'s status through exit() on OpenVMS

mariadb-admin, mariadb-dump, mariadb-check, mariadb-import and
my_print_defaults end main() with a return of their error code. Patch 0013
maps exit(n) to an error-severity status for DCL, but the C RTL hands
main()'s return value to DCL unchanged, so a failed run left $STATUS at
%X00000001: a mariadb-admin shutdown refused for lack of a password read as
success (PORTING_LOG, PLAN_SERVICE step 2). Under __VMS a small main() runs
the program's own, renamed vms_main(), through exit(), which covers every
return path (mariadb-import has five).

--- a/client/mysqladmin.cc	2026-10-07 03:44:47.562081583 +0100
+++ b/client/mysqladmin.cc	2026-10-07 03:44:47.640023920 +0100
@@ -322,6 +322,16 @@
 }
 
 
+#ifdef __VMS
+/*
+  OpenVMS: the C RTL passes main()'s return value to DCL as it is (1 is
+  success), while exit() goes through my_vms_exit() (my_global.h), which
+  gives a non-zero code an error status.  Run main() through exit().
+*/
+static int vms_main(int argc, char **argv);
+int main(int argc, char **argv) { exit(vms_main(argc, argv)); }
+#define main vms_main
+#endif
 int main(int argc,char *argv[])
 {
   int error= 0, temp_argc;
